<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!DOCTYPE plist PUBLIC "-//Apple//DTD PLIST 1.0//EN" "http://www.apple.com/DTDs/PropertyList-1.0.dtd">
<!--
    Entitlements for Transcripted Keyboard.app, the Writing input method nested at
    Contents/Library/Input Methods/ and signed with hardened runtime by build-beta.sh.

    Deliberately empty. The keyboard is a Developer ID IMKit input method outside the
    App Sandbox: macOS launches it from ~/Library/Input Methods, it reaches the app
    over a Unix-domain socket, and it links only system frameworks. None of that needs
    an entitlement. It never records audio, uses JIT, or loads other teams' libraries,
    so it gets none of the app's audio, JIT, or library-validation exceptions.

    If it ever moves into the App Sandbox, it will need com.apple.security.app-sandbox
    plus a com.apple.security.temporary-exception.mach-register.global-name entry for
    its InputMethodConnectionName, the way App Store input methods do.
-->
<plist version="1.0">
<dict/>
</plist>
